    "updated_at": "2022-02-03T23:30:28Z",
    "body": "Right, Bikeshed has the algo container scoping as a feature already, so I consider it reasonable to lean on that.\r\n\r\nBut in the absence of that as a feature in Wattsi, I (personally) think it's more valuable to have highlighted vars than to avoid over-highlighting vars. A week or two ago I was looking over an algo and had to read *very carefully* to see that a particular variable wasn't used anywhere else in the algo, an operation that would have taken half a second and been extremely reliable if I'd been able to just click on it and see if anything else colored.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
